## HTTP Status Codes Function

Here's a clean PHP function that returns an associative array mapping HTTP status codes to their descriptions:

```php
<?php

/**
 * Returns an associative array mapping HTTP status codes to their descriptions.
 *
 * @return array<int, string> Associative array of HTTP status codes and descriptions
 */
function getHttpStatusCodes(): array
{
    return [
        200 => 'OK',
        404 => 'Not Found',
        500 => 'Internal Server Error',
    ];
}
```

### Usage Examples

```php
<?php

// Get all status codes
$statusCodes = getHttpStatusCodes();
print_r($statusCodes);

// Look up a specific status code
$code = 404;
if (isset($statusCodes[$code])) {
    echo "Status {$code}: {$statusCodes[$code]}";
    // Output: Status 404: Not Found
}

// Iterate over all status codes
foreach ($statusCodes as $code => $description) {
    echo "HTTP {$code} - {$description}\n";
}
```

### Expected Output

```
Array
(
    [200] => OK
    [404] => Not Found
    [500] => Internal Server Error
)

Status 404: Not Found

HTTP 200 - OK
HTTP 404 - Not Found
HTTP 500 - Internal Server Error
```

